{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 11889,
    "dDurationMs": 4861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Prior to March 2020, there’s a good chance\nyou didn’t know what an N95 mask was, or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16750,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at least didn’t think about them unless\nyou were doing a home repair project with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19680,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lots of dust, or live in a part of the world\nwith crazy pollution or wildfire smoke."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24500,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And upon learning about them, you might think\n(like I did) that an N95 mask is basically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28970,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a really really fine strainer: a mesh of fibers\nwith gaps too small for dust and other airborne"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33430,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles to get through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34690,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A strainer filters out particles larger than\nits openings, and not particles smaller than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38340,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its openings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39340,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So with a mask you’d expect that after a\ncertain point, small enough particles will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42550,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sneak through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43550,
    "dDurationMs": 5590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this isn’t how N95 masks work: the particles\nthey filter are generally much smaller than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49140,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the gaps between fibers in the mask!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51200,
    "dDurationMs": 4569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What’s more, an N95 mask is actually really\nreally good at filtering both the largest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55769,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and smallest small particles -- it’s medium-sized\nsmall particles that are hardest for it to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60489,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61489,
    "dDurationMs": 5681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This isn’t at all like a strainer… because\nN95s are much cleverer than strainers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67170,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The overarching goal of an N95 mask is instead\nto get an airborne particle to touch a fiber"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72000,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the mask."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73000,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Regardless of how big an airborne particle\nis, once it touches a fiber, it stays stuck"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76860,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to it and doesn’t become airborne again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78840,
    "dDurationMs": 3470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This isn’t anything special about the fibers,\nbut about the size of the particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82310,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At a microscopic scale everything is sticky,\nbecause the weakly attractive force between"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86360,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "molecules IS strong enough to hold small things\nin place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90230,
    "dDurationMs": 3730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you shouldn’t think of N95 masks like\na fine window screen that keeps insects of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a certain size out; you should think of them\nmore like a sticky spider web that can catch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97560,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an insect of any size, as long as it touches\na strand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101040,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so N95 masks use a bunch of different\nclever physics and mechanical tricks to get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105810,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles to touch their fibers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107430,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, many spiderwebs are better than one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110470,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unlike strainers, where stacking many identical\nones doesn’t improve the filtering at all,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114420,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more layers of sticky fibers means more chances\nfor particles to get stuck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118940,
    "dDurationMs": 5370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And how likely particles are to hit or miss\na fiber depends in large part on their size."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124310,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Particles larger than a thousandth of a millimeter\nbasically travel in straight lines, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127850,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their inertia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128850,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because there are so many layers of fibers,\ntheir straight line paths are essentially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132070,
    "dDurationMs": 2830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "guaranteed to hit a fiber and stick."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134900,
    "dDurationMs": 3309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Airborne particles that are really really\nsmall are so light that collisions with air"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138209,
    "dDurationMs": 4021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "molecules literally bounce them around, so\nthey move in a random zig-zag pattern known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142230,
    "dDurationMs": 1369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as Brownian motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143599,
    "dDurationMs": 3491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This zig-zagging also makes it super likely\nthat a particle will bump into a fiber and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147090,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get stuck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148810,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Particles of in-between sizes are the hardest\nto filter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151410,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s because they don’t travel in straight\nlines, and they also don’t bounce around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154610,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "randomly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155610,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, they’re carried along with the\nair as it flows around fibers, meaning they’re"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159230,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "likely to get carried past fibers and sneak\nthrough even a mask with many layers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163480,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But N95 masks have a final trick up their\nsleeve."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165920,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They can attract particles of all sizes to\nthem using an electric field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170210,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the presence of an electric field even\nneutral particles develop an internal electrical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174340,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "imbalance which attracts them to the source\nof the field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176920,
    "dDurationMs": 2599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why neutrally-charged styrofoam sticks\nto an abused cat - I mean, a cat whose fur"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179519,
    "dDurationMs": 1041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been charged with static electricity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180560,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And how static electricity helps N95 mask\nfibers attract all particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181560,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But unlike a cat’s fur, an N95 mask’s\nelectric field isn’t just ordinary static"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186000,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electricity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187000,
    "dDurationMs": 4409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their fibers are like permanent magnets, but\nfor electricity: electrets!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191409,
    "dDurationMs": 3541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just like you can permanently magnetize a\npiece of iron by putting it in a strong enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194950,
    "dDurationMs": 4369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "magnetic field, you can ‘electretize’\na piece of plastic to give it a permanent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199319,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electric field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200769,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By electretizing the fibers in an N95 mask,\nthey gain a long-lasting ability to attract"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205739,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles, which means they capture about\n10 times as many particles as regular fibers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210769,
    "dDurationMs": 5921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is, after all, the point of an N95\nmask: filter out particles from the air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216690,
    "dDurationMs": 3469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By taking advantage of the molecular scale\nstickiness of matter, using many layers of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220159,
    "dDurationMs": 4201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fibers that catch straight-moving large particles\nas well as zig-zagging small particles, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224360,
    "dDurationMs": 4129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "having an electric field that attracts all\nparticles, you get a mask - not a strainer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228489,
    "dDurationMs": 5231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- that’s really good at trapping both small\nand large particles, and does a reasonably"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233720,
    "dDurationMs": 2849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "good job at filtering out middle sized particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236569,
    "dDurationMs": 4861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Precisely what fraction of those sneaky medium-sized\nparticles get blocked gives you the number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241430,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the mask - if at least 95% of those particles\nare filtered out, then the mask is rated N95."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248590,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, so N95 masks can be very effective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252870,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you’re a healthcare worker wearing\none of them, here are a few important things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256570,
    "dDurationMs": 2539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to look out for."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259109,
    "dDurationMs": 4041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The biggest influence on the performance of\nan N95 mask isn’t actually the mask - it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263150,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether you wear it properly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264200,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If a mask isn’t fully sealed on your face,\nair (\u0026 particles you’re trying to filter)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268970,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can just bypass the filter entirely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271330,
    "dDurationMs": 6019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dust, smoke, pollen, bacteria, and viruses\nall have different sizes, and so are filtered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277349,
    "dDurationMs": 2381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by N95 masks to different extents."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279730,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, germs for airborne illnesses don’t\nusually travel on their own – we breathe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284280,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or cough them out in droplets which have a\nwide range of sizes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287200,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the size of the virus or bacteria itself\nisn’t particularly relevant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292590,
    "dDurationMs": 5569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "N95 masks are intended to be disposable, but\nthe demand from COVID-19 has led to a global"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298159,
    "dDurationMs": 4721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shortage of N95 masks and the reality is that\nhealth workers have to reuse them - and thus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302880,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decontaminate them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s important to be aware that certain\nkinds of decontamination (for example, using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307960,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alcohol or liquids) can damage the electrostatic\nproperties of a mask and destroy their filtering"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312700,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ability, even if the mask appears visually\nunaffected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315610,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "N95decon is a volunteer team of scientists\ndeveloping and sharing research-based decontamination"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320860,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "methods so that masks can be reused during\nthis crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324090,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A big thanks to Brilliant for supporting this\nvideo - in this time of social isolation and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328700,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pandemic, the value of being versed in math\nand science is particularly evident, and Brilliant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333020,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continues to be a place you can go to learn\nand play with mathematical and scientific"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336160,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ideas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337160,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just today I exchanged emails with a viewer\nwho had a question about some special relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340510,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "calculations, and I recommended that they\ncheck out Brilliant’s introductory course"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343490,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on special relativity - there’s no better\nway to learn than by directly engaging with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347320,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "questions \u0026 problems!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349050,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brilliant also has fun daily challenges on\nvarious math, logic, science \u0026 engineering"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352800,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "topics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353800,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To learn more about Brilliant, go to brilliant.org/MinutePhysics\nand sign up for free; the first 200 people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359050,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will get 20% off an annual Premium subscription\nto all of Brilliant’s courses, quizzes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363140,
    "dDurationMs": 1070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and puzzles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364210,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to Brilliant for supporting MinutePhysics."
    } ]
  } ]
}
